Strong Final Interview Answer

A Snowflake Multi-Cluster Warehouse is an elastic compute configuration that automatically scales out by adding or removing compute clusters based on query concurrency. It is primarily designed to reduce query queuing and improve performance for workloads with many simultaneous users, such as BI dashboards and reporting systems. Multi-cluster warehouses are configured using MIN_CLUSTER_COUNT, MAX_CLUSTER_COUNT, and SCALING_POLICY parameters. STANDARD scaling prioritizes performance, while ECONOMY prioritizes cost savings. Unlike scaling up, which improves single-query performance, multi-cluster scaling mainly improves concurrency handling.

